NAME
    save - write a range of memory to a file

SYNOPSIS
    save path start end

DESCRIPTION
    Writes the bytes of memory in the half-open range [start, end) to a
    new file. start and end are hexadecimal addresses. save is an OS
    built-in command.

EXAMPLES
    save prog.bin 7A00 7C00

SEE ALSO
    load, dump, dep
